  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Sanitation Services for Internally Displaced Persons and Host Communities in Ma&apos;rib, Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) Cluster Strategy, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) seeks to contribute to safe and dignified living conditions by improving access to sanitation facilities and waste management services in target areas. The proposed intervention is in line with IOM&#x2019;s WASH Strategy in Yemen to implement solutions that are immediate, scalable and sustainable. IOM aims to support 185,178 individuals (direct and indirect beneficiaries), including direct support to 44,119 internally displaced persons, 2,937 host community members and 542 refugees under this intervention. IOM proposes to increase access to safe sanitation services in Ma&#x2019;rib for the most vulnerable crisis affected households through the construction and rehabilitation of latrines and cesspits, as well as support in faecal sludge and solid waste collection and garbage dump site improvement across sites in Ma&#x2019;rib, also increasing local capacity to provide sanitation services.</narrative>
  </description>
